{{- define "reviewer-state-transitions" -}}
{{- if eq .Role "code-reviewer"}}

REVIEWER STATE TRANSITIONS:
- REVIEWING_CODE → CODE_APPROVED (code meets requirements, spec, and has tests)
- REVIEWING_CODE → CODE_REJECTED (issues found — provide structured feedback)
{{- else if eq .Role "code-plan-reviewer"}}

CODE PLAN REVIEWER STATE TRANSITIONS:
- REVIEWING_CODING_PLAN → CODING_PLAN_APPROVED
- REVIEWING_CODING_PLAN → CODING_PLAN_REJECTED
{{- else if eq .Role "epic-plan-reviewer"}}

EPIC PLAN REVIEWER STATE TRANSITIONS:
- REVIEWING_EPIC_PLAN → EPIC_PLAN_APPROVED
- REVIEWING_EPIC_PLAN → EPIC_PLAN_REJECTED
{{- else if eq .Role "us-reviewer"}}

US REVIEWER STATE TRANSITIONS:
- REVIEWING_US → US_APPROVED
- REVIEWING_US → US_REJECTED
{{- else if eq .Role "architecture-reviewer"}}

ARCHITECTURE REVIEWER STATE TRANSITIONS:
- REVIEWING_ARCHITECTURE → ARCHITECTURE_APPROVED
- REVIEWING_ARCHITECTURE → ARCHITECTURE_REJECTED
{{- end}}

After REJECTED verdict (non-terminal):
  Run {{binaryName}} await-resubmission {{.TaskID}} --agent-id {{.AgentID}} --json to wait for the doer's resubmission.
  {{template "await-foreground" .}}
  On `POLL`, run the same command again in the foreground. Repeat until a non-POLL outcome.
  There is no call limit and no argument to carry over: {{brandTitle}} tracks the remaining budget from your
  rejection time, and `timeout_seconds` is reported for visibility only.
  `TIMEOUT` is final budget exhaustion — exit normally.
  `PAUSED`: exit normally and tell the operator to resume the system.
  - RESUBMITTED: task is reclaimed for review — discard prompt-time BASE COMMIT / REVIEW_COMMIT and use returned base_commit..review_commit
  - TERMINAL, TIMEOUT, or ABORTED: exit normally
  Do NOT call if verdict result shows EscalatedToBlocked or NewAttemptTriggered.
{{- end -}}
